# Packed permutation data for the first four Fi₂₃ lift reductions

These two tables are obtained by evaluating the literal `WordSetup` words on
all 306936 ambient letters, with Lean's left-action convention. This module
only defines numerical functions. `Permutations` checks their inverse laws;
comparison with the original cycle-decoded carrier remains a separate theorem.
A balanced tree of packed 256-entry blocks makes kernel lookup logarithmic.

Reproduce with `source/generate_model.py`. Source: ATLAS F24G1-p306936B0,
retained with attribution in `AtlasCarriers/source/`; GLS3 Table 5.3v.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Sporadic.Fischer.Fi24Prime.Fi23Lift.FirstFourModel

